🎯 Attack Logic (The Hacker's Trick)
The Blueprint: The attacker distributes a weaponized Excel Enabled Worksheet (.xlsm) named 
ORDER SHEET & SPEC.xlsm targeting remote workers. The document relies on heavy social engineering to force
the user to enable macros, triggering an automated multi-stage infection routine.

The Mechanism: The macro is split into several highly specialized subroutines designed to execute 
covertly:
Automated Execution & Replication: The Auto_Open routine triggers instantly upon file launch. 
It contains self-replication logic designed to extract the macro's own code and write it into separate files, 
acting like a network worm to infect other local documents.
Stager / Downloader: A dedicated subroutine (xdecd) dynamically reconstructs an obfuscated URL, uses 
system resources to download a second-stage malicious payload from a remote server, and saves it to the
local disk.
Execution & Living-off-the-Land: The macro invokes powerful Windows API functions, specifically ShellExecute 
and CreateObject, to quietly launch the downloaded payload without spawning visible windows.

Evasion Technique: The attack relies heavily on layers of defense evasion:
String Piecing: Crucial indicators (URLs, paths, API calls) are chopped into fragments and assembled at
runtime to break static string dump analysis.
Base64 Layering: A key execution variable (uiytvdverwt67fhrey) holds a Base64-encoded string linked to 
file-system operations.
Decoy Comments: The code is littered with fake code comments to confuse automated code-similarity scanners
and waste the analyst's time.

🕵️‍♂️ Investigation Process (How to Spot It)
Hash-Based Triage: Compute unique cryptographic signatures and query threat intelligence hubs (VirusTotal)
to map known vendor verdicts.
Behavioral Grouping: Isolate macro subroutines based on their structural role (Persistence, Network, Execution).
API Call Auditing: Track down the instantiation of high-risk administrative objects (CreateObject, ShellExecute).
Payload Extraction: Target the variables handling Base64 and network streams to reconstruct the final download 
URLs and execution paths.

